# The official Serve image digest pins the full transitive runtime. These are
# the overlay packages applied on top of it.
#
# The overlay used to RAISE the base (v1.29.0 shipped Docling 2.117 / Core
# 2.88). Since the base moved to v1.30.0 it does the opposite for one package:
# that image ships docling-core 2.91.0 and this pins it back to 2.90.0.
#
# On purpose. The point of the v1.30.0 bump was to take the jobkit
# heading-hierarchy fix, and holding docling-core still keeps that the only
# library change to attribute a behaviour difference to. Nothing is violated by
# doing so: docling-slim 2.118.0 asks for >=2.90.0 and docling-parse 7.10.0 for
# >=2.85.0, so `pip check` is satisfied. 2.91.0 carries one feature — uniform
# `source` on the `add_<...>` constructors — that this service does not call.
#
# Revisit when there is a reason to move Core, and re-measure the Stage A-D
# structure evidence when you do: docling-core is what defines DoclingDocument,
# and `groups[]`/`label`/`name`/parent chains are read directly by our
# provenance and container extraction.
docling-slim[standard,service-client,models-remote,format-opendocument]==2.118.0
docling-core==2.90.0
grpcio==1.67.1
